== A  CNOT in the target X-eigenbasis
CONFIRMED A1 [identity] CNOT = I (x) P+ + Z (x) P- (the owner's decomposition)
CONFIRMED A2c [countercontrol] countercontrol: I (x) P+ + X (x) P- is NOT CNOT (the sketch's erratum)

== B  the group generated by control rotations and CNOT
CONFIRMED B1 [identity] Ad(CNOT)(U (x) I) = U (x) P+ + ZUZ (x) P- for a generic U in SU(2)
CONFIRMED B2 [identity] the CNOT-conjugates of X(x)I, Y(x)I, Z(x)I are X(x)X, Y(x)X, Z(x)I
CONFIRMED B3 [identity] the Lie algebra generated is span{sigma(x)I, sigma(x)X}: closed under commutators (36 brackets exact) = su(2)(x)P+ + su(2)(x)P-
CONFIRMED B4 [identity] sigma(x)P+ and sigma(x)P- lie in that algebra: independent conditional rotations
MISMATCH B5 [identity] CNOT = [I(x)P+ + (-iZ)(x)P-] . [I(x)(P+ + iP-)], the first factor in SU(2)xSU(2) form, the second a target X-rotation by -pi/2 times a phase
CONFIRMED B6 [identity] the target rotation's sector blocks have determinants 1 and -1, which no global phase equalizes: it is not in Ad(SU(2)xSU(2)); CNOT adds a discrete element (the owner's precision)
CONFIRMED B7 [identity] V^-1 Z V Z for a real rotation V by a is the rotation by 2a: the second factor of the generated group contains all Y-rotations (and by symmetry all XY-plane rotations), hence all of SU(2)

== C  reachability of every pure state from a product under U(x)P+ + V(x)P-
CONFIRMED C1 [witness] 6 exact pure states (Bell, Gaussian-rational, a stage-3 witness) are each the image of a product state under an explicit U(x)P+ + V(x)P- with U, V in SU(2)
CONFIRMED C2c [countercontrol] countercontrol: Z(x)X commutes with CNOT, Rz on the control and Rx on the target, so <Z(x)X> is invariant under the commuting torus with cnot; a product |0>|0> has <Z(x)X> = 0 while the Bell state (|00>+|11>)/sqrt2 has <Z(x)X> = 0 too, but |0>|+> has 1: states with <Z(x)X> = 1 are unreachable from |0>|0> under that torus (reachability fails there, unlike C1)

== D  a control rotation carries the surgery defects out of their cones (exact witnesses)
MISMATCH D1 [witness] g = Ry(pi/4) on the control: phi = g psi_s has overlap <= 1/2 with every psi_t, so P_phi lies in K(Z_F) (PSD, pairs >= 0 with every defect), and ipW(P_phi, g e_s) = -1/2 < 0: g e_s is outside K(Z_F) = K(Z_F)* -- overlaps ['0', '0', '1/2 - sqrt(2)/4', 'sqrt(2)/4 + 1/2']
MISMATCH D2 [witness] the rotated negative eigenvector chi of E0 gives P_chi in K(E0) (ipW(P_chi, E0) >= 0) with ipW(P_chi, g E0) = -1 < 0: g E0 is outside K(E0) -- ipW(P_chi,E0) = -sqrt(2)/2
CONFIRMED D3c [countercontrol] countercontrol: ipW(e_t, g e_s) = |<psi_t|g psi_s>|^2/4 >= 0 for all s, t: the defect orbit pairs nonnegatively with itself, so the witness must be a pure state, as in D1

== E  the exclusion theorem's last step at the instance level
CONFIRMED E2 [identity] pure states pair nonnegatively with each other and are PSD: a cone containing all pure states contains Q3's extreme rays, hence Q3; with K = K* and Q3 = Q3*, K subset Q3* = Q3 follows (the owner's observation), so K = Q3

